WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.720
Is there any greater computer on Planet Earth
than the human brain?

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:10.130
That web of almost two hundred billion neurons
inside your skull gives you the equivalent

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.080
memory space of over a thousand one-terabyte
hard drives.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.180
Sure, the human brain might not be able to
process information at the speed of the average

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.619
computer, but it can regulate the movement
and functions of your entire body all while

00:00:24.619 --> 00:00:27.230
using less energy than a lightbulb.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:32.700
That’s right, our brains are pretty impressive
organic computers.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.280
But there is some stiff competition.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.469
Well not completely stiff.

00:00:37.469 --> 00:00:38.559
You’ll see.

00:00:38.559 --> 00:00:44.969
Say hello to SCP-003, also referred to as
the Biological Motherboard.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:50.739
Hearing that name, you would be right to assume
that SCP-003 is a computer formed of organic

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:55.539
components as opposed to man made microchips
and circuit boards.

00:00:55.539 --> 00:00:59.199
But there is a little bit more to it than
that.

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:08.920
SCP-003 is actually composed of two distinct
parts, referred to as SCP-003-1 and SCP-003-2,

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.430
both related but each with a separate origin.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.420
The former, 003-1, is the machine’s motherboard.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.780
Whereas your ordinary home computer or laptop
might have a motherboard made out of fiberglass

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.110
and copper, this one is far less conventional.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:28.410
So, what is 003-1 actually made from?

00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.420
The answer is living tissue.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.180
Everything from hair and fingernails, to chitin,
which is a substance found in the exoskeletons

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:38.280
of some invertebrate animals.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:43.590
All of these components, parts that may have
once belonged to a living thing, are arranged

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.530
in a configuration much like a computer’s
motherboard.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:51.660
It sounds like something plucked out of a
film by John Carpenter or David Cronenberg,

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.660
doesn’t it?

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:56.820
But how or why would someone ever construct
something like this?

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.870
Well, the answer to that isn’t clear.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:05.409
So far, the only answers we have come from
the SCP Foundation’s extensive testing of

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:07.390
the biological motherboard.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:14.020
According to researchers, SCP-003-1 predates
even the very earliest modern circuits by

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:19.810
several thousands of years, meaning that whoever
built it was certainly ahead of their time.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.349
Also, the motherboard is alive.

00:02:22.349 --> 00:02:25.579
Wait, did we forget to mention that?

00:02:25.579 --> 00:02:31.219
SCP-003-1 has displayed at least a low level
of sentience during testing by the Foundation,

00:02:31.219 --> 00:02:36.060
not enough to be considered an active threat
unless certain conditions make it dangerous.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:43.859
The second component of SCP-003 is 003-2,
a stone tablet that 003-1 was attached to

00:02:43.859 --> 00:02:45.599
when it was first discovered.

00:02:45.599 --> 00:02:51.420
The surface of 003-2 has had a number of runes
carved into it, but these symbols don’t

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.109
match letters or characters from any known
language.

00:02:55.109 --> 00:03:01.389
The runes on 003-2 are also known to regularly
emit a pale, flickering pattern of light.

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:06.099
Now, you’re probably asking, how is a slab
of stone able to light itself up?

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:13.129
Well, that is because SCP-003-2 has an internal
computer controlling it, and not one composed

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:16.180
of organic parts like hair and fingernails.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:22.469
Somewhere within the stone is a non-biological
computer, fueled by some unknown anomalous

00:03:22.469 --> 00:03:23.900
power source.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:29.279
The Foundation’s researchers can’t access
the internal components of SCP-003-2 without

00:03:29.279 --> 00:03:34.079
running the high risk of damaging it, but
as far as they can tell, whatever is running

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:38.510
this bizarre machine has been slowly losing
power for centuries.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.749
The Biological Motherboard is also known to
emit measurable levels of heat, light and

00:03:42.749 --> 00:03:45.120
radiations of an anomalous nature.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:49.549
So, why would someone go to the trouble of
creating a computer out of living parts and

00:03:49.549 --> 00:03:51.230
anomalous stone?

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:55.230
And what is the purpose of the Biological
Motherboard?

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:01.080
The SCP Foundation considers it highly probable
that the stone slab of 003-2 was actually

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:07.150
created with the intention of keeping the
motherboard component, 003-1, contained.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:11.739
Additionally, during testing, Foundation researchers
have been able to extract partially complete

00:04:11.739 --> 00:04:14.659
data from SCP-003.

00:04:14.659 --> 00:04:20.280
This data seems to refer to some sort of potential
catastrophe, either in the future or one that

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:25.600
has already occurred, as a direct result of
SCP-003-1.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:32.450
It would seem that 003-1 and 003-2 must stay
combined in order to prevent what the Foundation

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.750
would deem an LK Class Restructuring Event.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:39.340
How could the Biological Motherboard cause
an event like this?

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:43.020
It just sounds like a partially alive flesh
circuit on a stone slab?

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:48.971
It’s when the temperature around SCP-003
drops below thirty-five degrees Celsius, that

00:04:48.971 --> 00:04:51.910
things start to get really strange.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:56.901
From the minute they detect a decrease in
temperature, both components of SCP-003 begin

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.100
to react.

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:04.020
The biological motherboard itself starts to
grow, rapidly increasing its overall size.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:09.480
003-1 fuels this growth state by absorbing
any nearby matter, adding anything close enough

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.150
to its fleshy mass.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:16.370
First, it will assimilate any inorganic material,
everything from particles in the atmosphere

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.990
on up.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:23.190
003-1 transforms these new additions to itself
into the same organic matter that makes up

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:29.830
the biological motherboard, transforming metal
or plastic into dead skin cells, hair, chitin,

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:33.990
enamel, keratin, and other similar materials.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:40.370
This growth state increases until SCP-003
takes on a form in the shape of an ophiuroid,

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:46.540
also known as a brittle star: an aquatic lifeform
similar to a starfish, with five long, thin

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:49.430
appendages protruding from a central body.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:55.050
In the case of SCP-003, this “body” appears
to be the computer’s central processing

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.050
unit.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:06:00.980
In this new form, the biological motherboard
will also begin to create sensory organs that

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:05.020
will survey the area around it for more materials
to assimilate.

00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:11.380
Only 003-2, the stone slab, is immune to being
converted into biological matter.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:18.700
Next, the second phase of transformation occurs,
and SCP-003-1 begins to absorb organic matter

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.760
into its mass as well, living or otherwise.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:27.390
If you’ve ever seen The Blob, then you know
what this looks like… and how horrifying

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:32.340
it would be for any person unfortunate enough
to be standing too close.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:38.090
During this stage, SCP-003 will attempt to
copy the biology of a living organism it comes

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:43.600
into contact with, and uses this “template”
to try and lure others towards it.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:47.760
However, the Biological Motherboard appears
to use a lot of its processing power to analyze

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.220
and assimilate organic matter, and this can
actually diminish the speed at which it increases

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.220
size.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:00.930
So, what happens to 003-2, the stone component
of SCP-003, during all this?

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:05.550
When the biological motherboard is growing
and changing form, melding with other organisms

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:10.740
as its fleshy mass increases, does 003-2 power
its transformation?

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:14.390
No, in fact, it tries to prevent it.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:21.760
That’s right, the two components of SCP-003
do not work in tandem, they work against each

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:22.760
other.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:27.520
As the biological motherboard starts to grow,
the stone slab attached to it will emit concentrated

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.610
bursts of radiation.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:34.480
These radioactive emissions have a counteractive
effect on 003-1’s ability to assimilate

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:39.950
matter and increase its size, stopping the
organic mass of flesh from growing and even

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:45.670
reversing the process when the temperature
is raised to over one hundred degrees Celsius.

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:51.840
What we have so far is a machine in two parts;
one that grows and assimilates matter at lowered

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.450
temperatures, and the other that releases
radiation to stop this happening.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:02.181
Naturally, the SCP Foundation counteracts
the anomalous growing ability of 003-1 by

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:07.400
keeping the Biological Motherboard in a heated
containment environment, still attached to

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.700
003-2.

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:15.110
Under no circumstances is the temperature
of SCP-003’s containment unit to drop below

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:21.120
thirty-five Celsius, and normally no living
person is permitted to make any direct contact

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.300
with the machine.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:27.520
However, in the event of an emergency resulting
in loss of power, Foundation staff are required

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:32.300
to huddle skin to skin with the fleshy mass
of the motherboard, in an attempt to keep

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:37.430
it warm through their own body heat much like
how penguins huddle together for warmth.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:41.590
Of course, those unlucky members of personnel
probably hope they can generate enough heat

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:47.150
between them to keep 003-1 from starting to
grow, otherwise they know they’ll be the

00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:50.490
first that the biological motherboard will
absorb.

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:55.030
Should a member of personnel be chosen for
the particularly unpleasant task of being

00:08:55.030 --> 00:09:01.590
on hand to keep 003 warm, then they will be
made to submit for a full examination beforehand.

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:06.920
No one can be allowed close to SCP-003 if
they’re carrying any bodily parasites like

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:13.800
tapeworms or head lice, they would all be
extra organisms for 003-1 to absorb.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:19.250
Foundation staff are also required to be decontaminated
both before and after dealing directly with

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:21.350
SCP-003.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:26.691
And of course, no member of the SCP Foundation
is permitted to ever detach the biological

00:09:26.691 --> 00:09:29.350
motherboard from the stone component.

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:36.720
Given that 003-2 is the only device capable
of reducing and reversing SCP-003-1’s growth,

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.680
any changes in the pattern or color of its
glowing runes is to be reported to high ranking

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.130
members of the Foundation.

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:48.710
There have been multiple incidents involving
SCP-003 though, usually occurring when staff

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:53.850
working in the Foundation’s M03-Gloria research
team attempt to push the boundaries of the

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:56.380
device’s anomalous properties.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:10:00.980
Their interest in the Biological Motherboard
lies purely in seeing how the machine evolves

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:04.890
when allowed to grow beyond its second, brittle
star stage.

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:10.680
During one such incident, 003-1 was allowed
to grow and restructure for just over nine

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:16.010
minutes, after which the containment area’s
temperature was lowered and 003-2 released

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:19.170
a massive, continuous spike in radiation.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:23.740
Any of the new material that had been bonded
to the biological motherboard dissolved, falling

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:27.820
away and turning into a dusty residue which
was then collected for testing.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:35.820
At this point, both 003-1 and 003-2 seemed
to power down, with no detectable activity.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:41.120
The stone slab did not power back on until
it was connected to an external power generator.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:47.990
When the same procedure was repeated, and
003-1 re-entered its growth state, 003-2’s

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:51.680
radiation appeared to be unable to stop the
motherboard from increasing in mass.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:56.630
When it reached four times its original size
by assimilating any and all matter it could

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:03.800
reach, SCP-003 then began to change form in
a way that had never been observed before.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:09.660
Forming a protective shell around 003-1, the
entire living machine breached containment

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:15.850
into the observation area, grabbing M03-Gloria
researchers in its appendages.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:22.100
Using these M03-Gloria members, it began adding
to itself and forming a new body.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:27.880
As it assimilated the researchers, the Biological
Motherboard rearranged its center mass.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:34.030
SCP-003 then took on the form of a three-meter-tall
female humanoid, with tentacles protruding

00:11:34.030 --> 00:11:36.730
from its newly formed hair and spine.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:42.050
Next, the part-creature, part-machine began
to make indecipherable sounds, trying to communicate

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.300
with researchers through these rudimentary
vocalizations.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:50.240
Somehow, perhaps through information it had
absorbed from the researchers in its grasp,

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:54.490
SCP-003 wanted to speak.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.550
What happened next?

00:11:55.550 --> 00:12:00.310
An agent, sent on orders direct from the O5
Council, was dispatched to the containment

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:01.310
area.

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:06.210
According to Foundation records, the agent
attempted to engage in conversation with SCP-003’s

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:10.670
new form, but any data about their exchange
has been expunged.

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:16.540
Luckily, this agent was able to restore power
to SCP-003’s stone component, returning

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:21.750
the room temperature to the proper containment
levels which caused 003-1 to return to its

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.000
normal state.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:29.110
The threat re-contained, all nine members
of M03-Gloria were found to be unharmed, suffering

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:34.620
no side effects from assimilation, other than
a few cases of psychological trauma.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:39.870
One of them, Doctor Tilda Moose, the leader
of M03-Gloria, was later interviewed by the

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:40.870
Foundation.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:46.440
She claimed that SCP-003 had tried to talk
to the researchers, connecting with them mentally

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:49.800
in a crude, broken language that they couldn’t
understand.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:54.089
“She ripped three of the researchers apart
and put them back together unharmed.

00:12:54.089 --> 00:12:56.960
She doesn't understand human emotion, or pain.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.560
Or very much about how we experience the world.

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:03.300
Yes, I would say the containment procedures
are necessary.”

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:09.770
According to Doctor Moose, SCP-003 is some
unknown, alien entity, one without a clear

00:13:09.770 --> 00:13:11.770
understanding of humanity.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:17.600
It cannot understand pain or physical sensation,
yet it is bent on remaking the world into

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.600
a paradise.

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:21.500
“The whole effect felt like words of some
kind.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:26.290
I believe she wanted to see what we could
understand, so she could understand us,”

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.930
Doctor Moose said in her interview.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:30.470
“She didn't have time to finish analyzing
us.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:33.050
I don't know what would have happened if she
had.”

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:40.100
Now check out “SCP-001 - The Broken God
- Ouroboros Cycle” and “SCP-1461 - House

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:44.370
of the Worm” for more tales of anomalous
machines with minds of their own!

